The Sword of Ianna → Vector-06C
Copyright 2026 Boris Likhachev

This is a port of "The Sword of Ianna" (RetroWorks, 2017), MSX2 version.
Original game: code by Utopian (fjpena), graphics by Pagantipaco,
music by McAlby. Original source code and artwork:
https://github.com/fjpena/sword-of-ianna-msx2 — licensed under the Apache
License, Version 2.0.

Changes made in this port: the game logic is translated from the original Z80
source to Intel 8080 by tools/z80to8080.py and patched for the Vector-06C;
the screen output, input, floppy loader, quasi-disk layout and the Arkos
Tracker player for i8080 (src/vec/) are written anew; graphics, maps and
texts are converted by tools/data/; the menu, intro and level texts are
translated into Russian. The floppy loading screen is the loading screen of the
ZX Spectrum version (by MAC) redrawn for the Vector-06C 16-colour palette, with
the RetroWorks logo taken from the original menu screen.

The port is distributed under the same Apache License, Version 2.0 (see
LICENSE). Graphics, music and texts belong to the authors of the original
game.

Third-party files:
- tools/vendor/Z80.js — Z80 emulator by Molly Howell, MIT License.
- tools/bin/apultra — aPLib-format compressor by Emmanuel Marty and spke,
  zlib License.
- ref/cpc/ — release of the Amstrad CPC version by RetroWorks, with its own
  LICENSE file.
